    <b>Membership Policy</b><br><br>

                   1. Applicants must be of at least twenty levels to be considered for inclusion into
                   Temple of Dawn.<br><br>
                   2. Two members, or one officer must sponsor applicants. Sponsors must be in good
                   standing with the guild.<br><br>
3. Candidates should have grouped with ToD members before applying to the guild. This allows for us to get to know each other and makes 
the application process much easier.<BR><BR>
4. Once a new member has been accepted into the guild with the proper recommendations, they will remain be on a probationary period of 4 weeks. During this 4 week period, members will not be allowed to sponser other potential new recruits to the guild. Also during this period, any violations of guild policy may lead to expulsion from the guild without allowing for additional time to correct the behaviors. During the probationary period, second chances are unlikely to be granted.<br><br>

5. New members should send a blank e-mail to <a href=mailto:NewMembers@spasalon.com>Darkrok</a> for instructions on how to gain access to the boards, member list, etc.
<br><br>
6. New members will only be permitted to have one character in the guild during the probationary period, unless an officer specifically approves the addition. <br><br>

7. HOW TO APPLY FOR MEMBERSHIP:
<br><br>
Applicants wanting to be considered for guild membership need to post their intent to join on the open section of the bulletin board <a href=http://216.4.63.163/templebb/forumdisplay.cgi?action=topics&forum=Join+Temple+of+Dawn&number=12&DaysPrune=45&LastLogin= target=_blank>here</a>. <b>Please include name, race, class and level as well as reasons you have picked ToD to be your new home</b>.
Once this is done, applicants should actively seek out ToD members in which to group. Applicants names will be posted within the member only section of the bulletin board. ToD members will then make either positive or negative recommendations about the potential new inductee. Once we have the appropriate number of recommendations, you will be notified of the results by tell in the game.
